{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מורבכת", :translit "murbechat", :gloss "broad furnace"} {:he "רתחין", :translit "retachin", :gloss "boilers/roasters"} {:he "שחולטין אותה", :translit "shecholtin otah", :gloss "that roast it"} {:he "בותחין כל צרכה", :translit "botchin kol tzorkhah", :gloss "boiling all its need"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מורבכת", :b "רתחין"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 6:14 describes the meal-offering of the high priest, half offered in the morning and half in the evening, which must be eaten in a broad, deep pan called a machavat. Rashi on Leviticus 2:5, citing the Sifra, identifies the machavat as a deep vessel, distinct from a shallow marcheshet. Ba'al HaTurim applies the gematria of 'murbechat' equalling 'retachin' to explain that this vessel is designed to roast and boil the offering thoroughly.", :sources ["Leviticus 6:14" "Rashi on Leviticus 2:5" "Sifra on Leviticus 2:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "מורבכת", :a-value 668, :b "רתחין", :b-value 668, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:22:31.603371327Z", :model "glm-5.2"}